{"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A Gnusto game is one type conforming to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Game","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". That one type carries everything: the rooms and things, where they start, and the rules that govern them. This article is the model underneath — how the engine finds your declarations, how one value is both a declaration and a live reference, and how the world that never changes is kept apart from the state that does.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Declarations are stored properties","anchor":"Declarations-are-stored-properties","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Rooms, things, and custom state are declared as ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"stored properties","type":"text"}]},{"text":" of the game type:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["struct OperaHouse: Game {","    let foyer = Location { name(\"Foyer of the Opera House\") }","    let bar   = Location { name(\"Foyer Bar\"); dark }","    let cloak = Item { name(\"velvet cloak\"); wearable }","    @Global var disturbances = 0","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When you construct the world with ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameWorld\/init(game:saveDirectory:)"},{"text":", the engine’s bootstrap reflects over the game value with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Mirror"},{"text":" and collects every ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Global","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". It names each entity after the property it was stored in: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"foyer"},{"type":"text","text":" becomes "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/EntityID","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"foyer\""},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cloak"},{"type":"text","text":" becomes "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"cloak\""},{"type":"text","text":", and so on. You never write these IDs by hand — the property name "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"is"}]},{"type":"text","text":" the name."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is why declarations must live in the type’s main body, not an extension: Swift only allows stored properties there, and the Mirror only sees stored properties. (When even the declarations need to span files or ship separately, that is what a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameContent","isActive":true},{"text":" bundle is for — see ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ContentBundles"},{"text":".)","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"One value, two roles","anchor":"One-value-two-roles"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A declaration and a live reference are the ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"same value"}]},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let cloak = Item { name(\"velvet cloak\"); wearable }   \/\/ the declaration","","\/\/ …later, inside a rule body:","cloak.after(.take) {","    if cloak.isWorn { … }        \/\/ the live reference — reads current state","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cloak"},{"text":" is an ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item"},{"text":" value. Written in the game body it ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"declares"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" the cloak. Used in a rule it ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"reads and writes the live cloak’s state","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":": ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item\/isWorn"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item\/isHeld"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item\/name"},{"text":", and so on all consult the current turn.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This works because each ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location","isActive":true},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item","isActive":true},{"text":" mints a private identity token when it is created. The token — not the struct’s contents — is the entity’s identity, and it survives copying. Two items are equal when they share a token (","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item\/==(_:_:)","isActive":true},{"text":"). Inside a turn, the token resolves to the entity’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/EntityID","isActive":true},{"text":" and then to its state; outside a turn there is no state to read, so a live property access traps with an explanation rather than returning a meaningless value.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"References are always compile-checked. ","type":"text"},{"code":"cloak.after(.take)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"hook.holds(cloak)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"foyer.north(bar)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — every one is ordinary property access, so renaming a room or deleting an item breaks the build instead of the running game.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"The parts of the `Game` protocol","anchor":"The-parts-of-the-Game-protocol","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Game","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" gathers a handful of members, most with defaults so a small game declares only what it needs:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"title","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"intro","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"tagline","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxScore","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — the banner and scoring metadata.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"map","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — geography and initial placement, as a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WorldMap","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". Read once at startup to build the initial state.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rules"},{"type":"text","text":" — all game logic, as a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Rules"},{"type":"text","text":" value. Defaults to empty."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"verbs"},{"type":"text","text":" — player-typeable verbs this game adds, as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[SyntaxRule]"},{"type":"text","text":". Defaults to empty. See "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/AddingCustomVerbs"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"content"},{"text":" — content bundles the game composes itself from, as ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameContents","isActive":true},{"text":". Defaults to empty. See ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ContentBundles","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The protocol extension also hands every game three ambient references usable as bare identifiers inside "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"map"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rules"},{"type":"text","text":" blocks:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"player","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Player","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", for its location, score, and inventory, and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Player\/item","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for the player as a thing in the world (what ","type":"text"},{"code":"X ME","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" examines).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"world"},{"type":"text","text":" — the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/World","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", for rules that apply everywhere (like daemons)."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"command"},{"text":" — the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Command","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" currently being performed, inside a rule body.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"The `map` block","anchor":"The-map-block"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"map","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a result-builder property that yields a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WorldMap","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" — a flat list of ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/MapEntry","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" statements: exits, initial item placements, and the player’s start.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["var map: WorldMap {","    foyer.south(bar)                 \/\/ an exit","    bar.north(foyer)                 \/\/ and the way back, stated separately","","    player.starts(in: foyer)         \/\/ where the player begins","    cloak.startsWorn                 \/\/ where each thing begins","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Exits are one-way, so an asymmetric map needs no special case. There are five kinds of exit and eight ways to place a thing; ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WorldMapAndExits","isActive":true},{"text":" covers all of them.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Immutable definition, mutable state","anchor":"Immutable-definition-mutable-state"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Internally, the engine keeps two things strictly apart:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"definition","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is everything that never changes during play: names, descriptions, exits, rules, and the parser’s vocabulary. It is built once, from your declarations, at startup."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"state","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" is everything that "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"does"}]},{"type":"text","text":" change: where each item is, what is lit, the score, the turn count, which things have been touched, and your "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Global","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" values."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The entire mutable state is a single ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" value. Every change funnels through it, so a turn commits atomically at its end (see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TheTurnPipeline","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":") and save\/restore is a serialization call rather than a feature threaded through the codebase.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When you write "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cloak.isWorn"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"player.score += 1"},{"type":"text","text":" in a rule, you are reading and writing that one state value through the entity’s token — never touching the definition, and never seeing another turn’s half-finished changes."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"See-also","text":"See also"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GettingStarted"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TheTurnPipeline","isActive":true}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WritingRules","isActive":true}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}]}],"metadata":{"role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Gnusto"}],"title":"Anatomy of a Game","roleHeading":"Article"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/AnatomyOfAGame","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Essentials","title":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TheTurnPipeline"],"generated":true}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/gnusto\/anatomyofagame"]}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto"],["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/BootstrapDiagnostics"],["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WorldMapAndExits"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"How a single Swift type becomes a world the engine can run.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","references":{"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Item/isHeld":{"fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"isHeld","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/item\/isheld","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"True if the player is carrying the item (including worn items)."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item\/isHeld","title":"isHeld","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/GameContents":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"GameContents","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"GameContents","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","title":"GameContents","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The collected content bundles a game declares, in declaration order."}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/gamecontents","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameContents"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Location":{"type":"topic","title":"Location","abstract":[{"text":"A place in the world.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Location"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/location","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Location"}]},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/ContentBundles":{"type":"topic","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ContentBundles","title":"Content Bundles","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/contentbundles","abstract":[{"text":"Give a region its own declarations — its own type, and even its own package.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto":{"type":"topic","title":"Gnusto","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"An engine for writing interactive fiction in Swift.","type":"text"}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/GettingStarted":{"type":"topic","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GettingStarted","title":"Getting Started with Gnusto","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/gettingstarted","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Build and run your first text adventure, one piece at a time."}],"kind":"article"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/WritingRules":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/writingrules","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WritingRules","abstract":[{"text":"Attach game logic to items, locations, and the world.","type":"text"}],"title":"Writing Rules","type":"topic","kind":"article","role":"article"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/World":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/World","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"World"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"World"}],"title":"World","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/world","abstract":[{"text":"Rules that apply everywhere, declared through the ","type":"text"},{"code":"world","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" identifier in a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"rules","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" block:","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Item/==(_:_:)":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item\/==(_:_:)","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"==","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"Item","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto4ItemV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Item","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto4ItemV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"title":"==(_:_:)","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/item\/==(_:_:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Two items are equal when they share the same declaration identity."}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Game":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Game"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Game"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/game","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A complete game: declarations, geography, and rules."}],"title":"Game","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Game","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/WorldMap":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WorldMap","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"WorldMap"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"WorldMap"}],"title":"WorldMap","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/worldmap","abstract":[{"text":"The geography and initial placements of a game, declared in one block:","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Rules":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Rules"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Rules"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/rules","abstract":[{"text":"The collected rules of a game, declared in one ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rules"},{"text":" block. Large games","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"compose: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"var rules: Rules { cloakRules; barRules }"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"title":"Rules","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Rules","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/GameWorld/init(game:saveDirectory:)":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"convenience"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"game"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto4GameP","text":"Game","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"saveDirectory","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation3URLV","text":"URL","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/gameworld\/init(game:savedirectory:)","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Builds the world from a game definition, validating it up front."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The random stream is seeded fresh each run; use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init(game:seed:)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to replay a specific one."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameWorld\/init(game:saveDirectory:)","title":"init(game:saveDirectory:)","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Item":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A thing in the world."}],"title":"Item","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Item"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/item","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"Item","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Item/name":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"name"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/item\/name","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The item’s display name."}],"title":"name","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item\/name","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Command":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Command"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Command"}],"type":"topic","title":"Command","abstract":[{"text":"A parsed player command, available inside rule bodies as ","type":"text"},{"code":"command","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/command","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Command"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Item/isWorn":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"isWorn"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/item\/isworn","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"True if the player is wearing the item."}],"title":"isWorn","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnu